<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74896" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρημι</span></b> , 
			Aeol.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁράω,</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Sapph.
			2.11
		</span></i> ; 3sg.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					30.22
				</span></i>
			, cf. 
				Aeol.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπόρημι</span>; part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pittac.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				1.81
			</span></i> ; to this athematic stem <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρη-</span> (not from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρα-</span>)
			prob. belong 2sg.
			
				Med.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρηαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.343
				</span></i>
			 and 2sg.
			
				Act.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποθόρησθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					6.8
				</span></i>
			 :—but many 
				Dor.
			 forms have <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span> by 
				contr.
			 from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰε</span>, as 
				Lacon.
			
			inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					1077
				</span></i>
			, Syrac. imper. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					170.12
				</span></i>
			, etc. ; 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁράω.</span>
			</div>
